| Parameter | Value | Basis |
|---|---|---|
| Scale | 2,800 sellers; 4,000 products; 20,553 competitions; 14 days | **Documented** (20,553 competitions, 2,766 sellers); products and keywords are ours |
| Related sellers | 2 special merchants, lifetime ratings 620,000 and 410,000; present in 93% of products | Our assumption (Cloudtail and Appario are named in the paper) |
| Seller types | 2 related, 560 FBA, 2,238 merchant-fulfilled (FBM) | Our assumption |
| Strike-through | Related 77%, FBA about 70%, FBM about 2% of low-rated reviews | **Documented** overall: 74.13% for Amazon-fulfilled sellers |
| Hidden winner rule | −7 × price gap + 0.9 × fast + 4 × reported positive + 0.30 × log10(ratings) + 0.45 × related + Gumbel noise (0.35) | Our assumption, calibrated to 87.74% win and 29.15% out-of-position |
| Survey | 5 groups × 50 participants × 15 tasks; logit utility with participant effect; 60 tasks where a related seller won without the lowest price | **Documented** design; utility weights calibrated to the documented shares |
| DQ issues | 300 duplicate offer rows, 60 price decimal slips (×10), 2% missing shipping fee | Built-in messiness |

